& [RuntimeIdentityAndABI] binds the proved forms
  + runtime consumes and emits the exact supported CTPR form and profile versions
  + unsupported versions require an explicit migration result or typed refusal
  + every input validates before transition evaluation
  + DeterministicRuntimeRoot contains explicit profile, policies, LogicalClock, FakeRepository, optional Calendar and Planner projections, lane sessions, compiler fixtures, bounds, and trace frontier
  + no ambient singleton, global canonical state, external handle, or hidden cache has authority

& [TransitionContract] is functional
  + RuntimeOperation is a closed tagged union with caller, expected root digest, exact inputs, policy, and bounds
  + evaluation returns RuntimeReceipt or RuntimeFault and at most one immutable successor root
  + accepted receipts bind operation, before and after digests, logical time, emitted identities, trace, bounds, and disposition
  + refused and faulted operations do not partially admit successor state
  + prior root values remain unchanged and replayable

& [DeterminismAndBounds] are mandatory
  + same normalized root, operation, exact profiles, and policy produce the same normalized result and semantic trace
  + stable declared ordering applies to maps, sets, graphs, events, messages, traces, and serialization
  + time, ordering, horizon, event, recurrence, graph, lane, trace, text, byte, and fixture bounds are explicit
  + randomness, system clock, locale default, environment, thread schedule, hash iteration, filesystem order, network, and provider state are absent
  + bound exhaustion is a typed fail-closed result
  - never: infer truth, correctness, safety, priority, consent, or authority from determinism

& [FakeRepository] is the append-only reference state
  + stores RepositoryGenerations, MaterialEvents, ContentObjects, SemanticSnapshots, derived indexes, branch heads, and merge predecessors in memory
  + compare-and-append requires exact expected predecessor and rejects stale, forked, missing, or inconsistent frontiers
  + admitted logical ordering comes from explicit input and policy
  + content digest is verified over supplied bytes or normalized value without filesystem access
  + snapshot declares exact semantic event frontier and never claims simultaneous external-world capture
  + derived indexes cite source generation, are deterministically rebuildable, and never replace semantic authority
  + rejection, supersession, branch, merge, compaction, and preserved-unrelated evidence remain explicit

& [LogicalTime] is supplied transition state
  + LogicalClock is immutable caller-controlled counter or ordered token
  + it advances only by an accepted operation
  + fixture civil time requires declared timezone, calendar, precision, and interpretation policy
  + physical and provider time are absent
  + record order and timestamp alone cannot prove causality

& [FakeCalendar] separates temporal identities
  + stores immutable CalendarItem revisions, WakeConditions, recurrence policies, exceptions, occurrences, commitments, lifecycle, and simulated provider placeholders
  + recurrence expansion is deterministic, exception-aware, and horizon-bounded
  + due, missed, cancelled, completed, and superseded states evaluate against supplied time and emit material event candidates
  + wake emits only a reentry candidate after exact task, plan, repository, capsule, policy, and authority revalidation
  + schedule, commitment, provider synchronization, notification, and execution are distinct
  - never: infer priority, truth, consent, permission, or action from a date or due state

& [DeterministicPlanner] constructs bounded proposals
  + validates TaskContract, exact predecessor PlanRevision, repository generation, Calendar view, policies, resources, and proof gates
  + dependency DAG cycles or unresolved required identities return witnesses
  + candidate selection follows declared priority policy then stable identity tie-break
  + result preserves alternatives, assumptions, uncertainty, proofs, stop, and reroute conditions
  + Schedule output remains a proposal until separate commitment authority
  - never: admit successor repository state, grant authority, commit a calendar item, or execute work

& [Materiality] classifies candidate events
  + policy and version determine durable, aggregate, transient, or rejected disposition
  + classification records the exact rule and cannot rewrite prior history
  + aggregation states coverage, count, method, loss, and retained rehydration evidence

& [TandemAndCapsules] implement the reflective walk
  + ChangeCapsule lifecycle transitions require exact predecessor generation and canonical legal edge
  + prospective preparation pins task, plan, repository, capsule, target, expected transform, effects, proof, and unrelated-state exclusion
  + ExecutionLane accepts supplied simulated observation records only and performs no effect
  + RetrospectiveLane returns evidence, objections, uncertainty, invalidation, residuals, and candidate disposition for the exact generation
  + LaneMessages are immutable, named, versioned, causally referenced, logically ordered, and explicitly acknowledged
  + ObserverJoin refuses missing, stale, wrong-subject, wrong-generation, incompatible-policy, unmet-proof, or unaccounted-diff inputs
  + ReleaseBarrier opens only for the exact named dependency and receipt set
  + timeout, cancellation, lag, crash reentry, and residual are logical state transitions without threads or timers

& [CompilerDiffFixture] is bounded correspondence evidence
  + fixed source, SemanticIR, BuildIR, target metadata, impact, diff, correspondence, diagnostic, and proof records are data
  + forward fixture predicts identities, dependencies, diagnostics, invalidation, target metadata, and proof needs
  + an independently implemented rear fixture compares exact before and candidate generations
  + checked requires complete declared diff classes, explicit unknowns, independent correspondence, and Observer disposition
  + mismatch invalidates exact affected results while preserving declared unrelated state
  - never: claim a general parser, compiler, target backend, executable artifact, or target self-certification

& [FaultAndVersionContract] fails closed
  + faults include invalid form, unsupported version, stale predecessor, missing ref, duplicate identity, cycle, bound, recurrence horizon, wake mismatch, illegal transition, missing return, wrong generation, incomplete diff, missing correspondence, forbidden effect, nondeterminism, and internal invariant
  + every fault binds operation, subject, expected, observed, evidence, safe residual, and trace location
  + exact-version is the first-profile default; migration is a separate deterministic transform with loss and proof

& [AuthorityAndEffectBoundary] is strict
  + allowed reads are exact supplied in-memory values
  + allowed writes are returned immutable values, receipts, traces, and faults
  + no filesystem, network, database service, system clock, process, thread, provider, notification, Git, model, procedure interpreter, unsafe code, device, or external effect
  + simulated observations and provider placeholders are data and confer no effect claim

& [FirstImplementationFrontier] may be separately claimed after phase-lock validation
  + CDRA-I01 through CDRA-I07 in the plan define bounded dependency-ordered Rust library and test slices
  + WS-CTPR-011 through WS-CTPR-013 may be reconciled to those slices only within this exact authority
  + implementation must begin with root, operation, receipt, fault, bounds, and transition dispatcher
  + each slice requires a separate worker claim and completed-work review
  + no live integration or effect frontier is released

& [RequirementSet] is canonical
  + forty requirements are individually mapped
  + specification status is satisfied after exact phase-lock validation
  + runtime implementation and test evidence remain not started

